framework DecisionAudit

domain PlanReviewMutationCore:
  description "Implementation decision for PLAN_REVIEW_MUTATION_CORE"

problem P1:
  "How should private Grammar 10 Plan Review create and resolve mutation compose existing plan mutation guards while preserving one candidate and the unchanged public surface?"

step S1:
  premise PR1:
    "The accepted contract requires closed preview-first create and resolve requests, exact replay behavior, a distinct Plan Review authority decision, semantic basis checks, one final candidate, and safe persistence"

step S2:
  evidence EV1:
    "The accepted source core parses and formats identity-checked Grammar 10 requests, projects the closed Plan Review basis and review state, and keeps all of those APIs private"
    resource:
      file "src/plan-review/source.ts"
      label "Grammar 10 source boundary"
    resource:
      file "src/plan-review/basis.ts"
      label "Semantic basis boundary"

step S3:
  evidence EV2:
    "The source lexical layer masks every Plan Review declaration with byte-position-preserving comments; lowering the two-digit Grammar 10 version to the one-digit Grammar 9 version creates one known offset delta for all later edits"
    resource:
      file "src/plan-review/source-lexical.ts"
      label "Plan Review masking"
    resource:
      file "src/temporal-schedule/source-lexical.ts"
      label "Position-preserving masking primitive"

step S4:
  evidence EV3:
    "The current Contract 10 batch planner already composes the active mutation, governance, assurance, milestone-acceptance, and validation behavior and returns normalized edits plus one digest-bound candidate"
    resource:
      file "src/application/contract10-runtime.ts"
      label "Current batch planner"

step S5:
  evidence EV4:
    "The Node Host already exposes optimistic-locking validated create and replace operations through the SafePersistencePort"
    resource:
      file "src/ports/node-host.ts"
      label "Safe persistence boundary"

step S6:
  decision D1 based_on P1, PR1, EV1, EV2, EV3:
    "Implement a private Plan Review planner that normalizes closed create and resolve requests, handles exact replays before candidate construction, masks Review declarations for the injected Grammar 9 batch planner, and maps its edits back across the one-character version delta"

step S7:
  decision D2 based_on PR1, EV1, D1:
    "Create inserts one canonical request declaration; plan_retained appends resolution evidence only when before and final semantic basis digests are equal; plan_changed requires the composed batch to succeed and requires unequal before and final basis digests"

step S8:
  decision D3 based_on PR1, EV3, D1, D2:
    "For plan_changed, apply the existing batch edits and the non-overlapping Review resolution edit to the original source, validate the complete Grammar 10 candidate once, preserve the existing composed result and diagnostics, and fail with PTREV-109 when its independent guards do not succeed"

step S9:
  decision D4 based_on PR1, EV1, D2, D3:
    "Evaluate the distinct PlanReviewAuthorityDecision v1 against the original effective DAG owner and delegates, bind it to source and complete candidate digests, and accept a non-direct actor only when the exact owner is in the fresh request assertions"

step S10:
  decision D5 based_on PR1, EV1, D1:
    "Normalize the closed plan_changed batch request with RFC 8785 JSON and store its SHA-256 digest; an already resolved request compares normalized resolution fields and digest and returns before applying any later source mutation"

step S11:
  decision D6 based_on PR1, EV4, D3, D4:
    "Expose private persistence helpers that accept only successful authorized digest-bound candidates, revalidate Grammar 10 through SafePersistencePort, and retain output and in-place optimistic-lock behavior"

step S12:
  decision D7 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6:
    "Focused acceptance covers closed input normalization, create replay and conflict, direct and confirmed authority, retained and changed basis rules, composed-guard failure, changed replay mismatch, one-candidate edit composition, stale expected digest, and unchanged public exports"

step S13:
  pending PD1:
    "Public CLI commands, schemas, Next integration, lifecycle and advance behavior, plan task status, commit, push, release, and Issue mutation remain separate"
